  "rationale": "Evidence: iteration 7 (kd 0.8, kp 3.5) is the best raced design at 304.77. The oval finishes in 13 of 20 trials, but the s-bend and slalom still end off track, with steering_oscillation at 0.23 and 0.25. Iteration 8 (kp 3.0) lowered the score to 296.66 and did not clear the bends, so kp is not the lever to push further. Following the Evaluator's requested revision, I change one variable: controller.kd from 0.8 to 1.0. Geometry (sensors at y = 0.07, x = -0.04 to +0.04, sensor_size 0.012), kp 3.5, base_speed 1.6, sensor_weights and line_loss last_direction stay unchanged, so the race isolates the derivative effect. Expected result: steering_oscillation on the s-bend and slalom falls below 0.23 and progress on those tracks rises above 0.30 and 0.19, while oval finishes hold at 13 of 20 or better. Hypotheses: (H1) more damping reduces the jitter that drives the bend failures; (H2) if the score falls below 304.77 or oval finishes drop below 13 of 20, kd is past its useful range, and the Evaluator's fallback is the kd 0.8 build (iteration 7); (H3) if the robot stays on track on all tracks but misses the 3.0 s limit, base_speed is the next lever, to be raised toward 1.8 in a later iteration. Measurements wanted: completion, progress, completion_time, rms_error, max_error, line_loss_events, steering_oscillation and controller_errors on all three development tracks.",
